fr:mainmatter.html:p:
If the angular frequencies are different, the resultant displacement changes with time. For instance, given x_1 = A_1\cos (\omega _1t+\phi _1) \\ x_2 = A_2\cos (\omega _2t+\phi _2)
the resultant displacement is
A = \sqrt {A_{1}^{2}+A_{2}^{2}+2A_{1}A_{2}\cos ((\omega _{2}-\omega _{1})t+\phi _{2}-\phi _{1})}

The wavelength \lambda  of a sinusoidal waveform traveling at constant speed v is given by

    \lambda  = vT = \frac {v}{f}

where f is the frequency of the wave and T is the period of the wave.
